index b0e977e..0987127 100644
--- a/packages/mermaid/src/docs/config/usage.md
+++ b/packages/mermaid/src/docs/config/usage.md
@@ -1,5 +1,21 @@
 # Usage
 
+## Experimental flowchart source maps (v<MERMAID_RELEASE_VERSION>+)
+
+Pass `{ sourceMap: true }` as the fourth argument to `mermaid.render` to receive a source map alongside the SVG:
+
+```js
+const { svg, sourceMap } = await mermaid.render('diagram', code, undefined, { sourceMap: true });
+const piece = sourceMap.pieces[0];
+const selectedSource = sourceMap.source.slice(piece.span.start, piece.span.end);
+```
+
+The map contains the exact original source and separate node/edge occurrences. Spans are zero-based UTF-16 offsets with an exclusive end; optional `labelSpan` selects label content. Repeated node references share a semantic identity but retain separate spans. Node `domId` identifies the suffix of the rendered node ID (`diagramId + '-' + domId`); edge `domId` matches the edge's `data-id`. Edges also include `from` and `to` node identities. The map is a source projection, not a complete editable AST.
+
+This initial implementation supports plain flowcharts, including CRLF and comments. Mapped rendering rejects frontmatter, directives, HTML/entities/Markdown labels and shape metadata. Groups, styling and accessibility text do not have mapped occurrences. Unsupported diagrams and preprocessing throw instead of returning approximate positions. Rendering without the option retains existing behavior and returns no `sourceMap` property.
+
+The option does not alter the SVG or install event handlers. Applications can serialize mapping data or implement selection separately. The mapping API is experimental.
+
 Mermaid is a JavaScript tool that makes use of a Markdown based syntax to render customizable diagrams, charts and visualizations.
 
 Diagrams can be re-rendered/modified by modifying their descriptions.
